{:edb/db-before-t 1118 :edb/db-after-t 1119 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534431 50 #inst "2026-10-07T03:09:29.016Z" 13194139534431 true] [17592186119876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287942 13194139534431 true] [17592186119876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287946 13194139534431 true] [17592186119877 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287930 13194139534431 true] [17592186119878 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287937 13194139534431 true] [17592186119878 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287949 13194139534431 true] [17592186287930 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287931 13194139534431 true] [17592186287930 1089 "q-107070" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287930 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534431 true] [17592186287930 1100 "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{(x-5)({x}^{3}+1)}{{x}^{2}-4x-5}.$" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287930 1113 #uuid "1a5fa7c7-9fbe-52bd-ba66-480727f1d2f6" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287930 1145 "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-5)({x}^{3}+1)}{{x}^{2}-4x-5} & =\\frac{(x-5)(x+1)({x}^{2}-x+1)}{(x-5)(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x-5)(x+1)}({x}^{2}-x+1)}{\\cancel{(x-5)(x+1)}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=-1,$ and $x=5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/assets/bca412e444ba3f3126cc88394ea466c48c2dcb60916dcf42ffb0abecb2c5ad48.png)" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287932 13194139534431 true] [17592186287931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287933 13194139534431 true] [17592186287931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287934 13194139534431 true] [17592186287931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287935 13194139534431 true] [17592186287931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287936 13194139534431 true] [17592186287931 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534431 true] [17592186287931 1041 "selection" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287931 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287932 13194139534431 true] [17592186287931 1110 #uuid "905974fd-26d5-5b35-a2f1-07129d050534" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287932 1034 "No vertical asymptotes" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287932 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534431 true] [17592186287932 1111 #uuid "2a0d83d8-da8f-52f9-b429-67c1f860461f" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287933 1034 "x=-1" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287933 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534431 true] [17592186287933 1111 #uuid "2ee9654b-30ad-50a7-8a2f-6805b51ea5a5" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287934 1034 "x=0,5" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287934 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534431 true] [17592186287934 1111 #uuid "30b5815a-645a-5fd7-b3af-3ce38e365c67" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287935 1034 "x=5" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287935 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534431 true] [17592186287935 1111 #uuid "a753f6f7-9b7e-5f68-a919-5f662daff4b4" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287936 1034 "x=-1,5" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287936 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534431 true] [17592186287936 1111 #uuid "a33ccc23-64f3-5421-9df5-a7d3ec6627d0" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287937 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287938 13194139534431 true] [17592186287937 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287940 13194139534431 true] [17592186287937 1089 "q-339769" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287937 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534431 true] [17592186287937 1100 "From **left to right**, the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x-3}-\\frac{1}{x+7}$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}} \n$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139534431 true] [17592186287937 1113 #uuid "671ca5d9-901c-5af2-b9e3-c730af413330" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287937 1145 "First, let's put the two terms over a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x-3}-\\frac{1}{x+7} & =\\frac{x+7-(x-3)}{(x-3)(x+7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{(x-3)(x+7)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we proceed to set the denominator equal to zero and get\n\n$$\n(x-3)(x+7)=0\\,⟹\\,x=-7\\,,\\,x=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the vertical asymptotes are at $x=-7$ and $x=3.$" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287939 13194139534431 true] [17592186287938 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534431 true] [17592186287938 1041 "field-1" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287938 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287939 13194139534431 true] [17592186287938 1110 #uuid "9483d567-cc86-578e-b2bd-2a5a3331dae6" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287939 1034 "-7" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287939 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534431 true] [17592186287939 1111 #uuid "07db8baa-617a-5396-9f9e-d4d03ab0a471" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287941 13194139534431 true] [17592186287940 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534431 true] [17592186287940 1041 "field-2" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287940 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287941 13194139534431 true] [17592186287940 1110 #uuid "cf9aa334-76cf-5e3b-bc80-e119ca2474eb" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287941 1034 "3" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287941 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534431 true] [17592186287941 1111 #uuid "3c7ba1b0-035c-5406-a080-9225980249ed" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287942 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287943 13194139534431 true] [17592186287942 1089 "q-339963" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287942 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534431 true] [17592186287942 1100 "The vertical asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{10x}{{x}^{2}+5x}$ is\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534431 true] [17592186287942 1113 #uuid "1a5b1368-2d7a-5777-a440-5ec5215cbc5f" 13194139534431 true] [17592186287942 1145 "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10x}{{x}^{2}+5x} & =\\frac{10x}{x(x+5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\cancel{x}}{\\cancel{x}(x+5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{x+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$